  (text "Coin sorter HAT+ - rev 0 sketch (2026-09-18). Connectivity is by global labels; redraw with wires as you like.\nFootprints reference the stock KiCad 8 libraries: run Tools > Update PCB from Schematic to pull them into coin_hat.kicad_pcb.\n\nPICO PIN MAP            UART0 GP0/GP1 <-> Pi GPIO14/15 (/dev/ttyAMA0, dtparam=uart0=on). REPL stays on USB.\n belt     STEP GP2  DIR GP3  EN GP4    (unchanged from today's firmware)\n diverter STEP GP6  DIR GP7  EN GP8    (17HS4023 on U4, TMC UART addr 2)\n feeder   STEP GP18 DIR GP19 EN GP22   (TMC UART addr 1; belt is addr 0)\n TMC UART GP20 TX via 1k / GP21 RX on the single-wire bus   |   home switches GP10/GP11   |   coin sensor GP5\n key light MOSFET GP14   aux MOSFET GP15   ring data GP16 (74AHCT1G125 -> 5 V)   VMOT sense GP28 (100k/15k)\n\nPI RESETS THE PICO: GPIO17 high -> Q3 pulls RUN low. Active-high so the Pi's default pull-down on GPIO17 leaves the Pico running.\n  pinctrl set 17 op dh; sleep 0.1; pinctrl set 17 dl      (replaces the USB DTR trick that relaunches main.py)\n\nPOWER: 12 V jack -> F1 -> +12V bus (drivers, switched outputs) -> U5 buck -> +5V -> Pi header pins 2/4 and Pico VSYS via D1.\n  Pi 5 fed over the header skips USB-PD: add usb_max_current_enable=1 to config.txt if USB peripherals need >600 mA.\n  Size F1 to the real load: Pi 5 ~2.3 A at 12 V worst case + three motors.\n\nDRIVER SOCKETS take TMC2209 or A4988 - set the 4 solder jumpers per socket (JPx1..4):\n  TMC2209: JPx3=A (pin4 on the UART bus), JPx4=A (CLK to GND), JPx1/JPx2 = UART address (belt 00, feeder 10, diverter 01).\n           Current set in software. StallGuard on DIAG (not on the 16-pin socket on all breakouts) can home the diverter.\n  A4988:   JPx3=B (MS3 high), JPx4=B (RESET tied to SLEEP), JPx1+JPx2 closed = 1/16 step. Set Vref = I x 8 x Rsense\n           (R100 sense: 0.40 V for 0.5 A on the 17HS4023). Heatsink.\n\nVERIFY BEFORE ORDERING: TMC2209 breakout pin order, buck module pin order, HAT+ header/hole positions against the\n  Raspberry Pi HAT+ mechanical spec, and header height vs the Pi 5 active cooler (use an extra-tall stacking header)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 105 5 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left top)) (uuid "df5c71e0-16cf-495f-bb4b-fdb389379f4d"))
